From: (local patch, not an upstream commit) QM1 Debian Maintainers <qm1-debian@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: rtw88: ps: Trigger firmware recovery when failing to leave LPS state

Carried from the upstream rtw-next commit

  dc16902cad9c6b08df9395a510c7be44fbab545d
  "wifi: rtw88: ps: Trigger firmware recovery when failing to leave LPS state"
  (Kalpesh Solanki, 2026-11-03)

which is *not* part of the upstream snapshot this module is built from
(05441d697f7f9a927264f4058cbbc6a03dfcac9d, a torvalds/linux master
snapshot of 2026-11-03): master only merged rtw-next up to the
"rtw-next-2026-10-08" tag, so every 8723B fix from 2026-10-09 onwards
is missing from the tree we ship.

Why we carry it:

When the firmware fails to leave the low power state, the driver only
logged a warning and cleared REG_TCR.  The chip was then left in a state
where later H2C commands fail and TX traffic hangs indefinitely -- the
firmware never comes back on its own.  That is exactly the "the link
dies and never returns" class of failure this machine keeps hitting, and
this box has no wired network to fall back to.

The upstream fix calls rtw_fw_recovery() on that path, so the driver
resets the hardware and re-syncs by itself.

Note on why this was previously listed as "not needed": the shipping
module configures rtw88 with disable_lps_deep only.  The parameter set
rtw_power_mgnt / rtw_smart_ps / rtw_ips_mode belongs to the in-tree
staging driver (r8723bs), rtw88 does not have them, and
disable_lps_deep only turns off the *deep* low power mode.  The ordinary
LPS leave path is still reachable, so the path this fix protects is
reachable in the configuration we ship.
diff --git a/ps.c b/ps.c
--- a/ps.c
+++ b/ps.c
@@ -166,6 +166,7 @@
 		rtw_write32_clr(rtwdev, REG_TCR, BIT_PWRMGT_HWDATA_EN);
 		rtw_warn(rtwdev, "firmware failed to leave lps state\n");
 		rtw_fw_dump_dbg_info(rtwdev);
+		rtw_fw_recovery(rtwdev);
 	}
 }
 
